meta {
  name: Kill run
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/runs/:run_id/kill
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  run_id: {{runId}}
}

docs {
  Terminate an in-flight run. The kill signal flows through the executor's
  per-run watch channel and tears down the active step's process tree
  (cross-platform: SIGTERM/SIGKILL on Unix, taskkill /T on Windows).

  Remaining steps in the workflow are skipped unless `always_run: true`.
  The run's terminal status is `Killed`.

  Response: **202 Accepted** with body `{ "message": "Kill signal sent" }`. The signal is best-effort; the actual run may take additional time to terminate. If the run is already terminal (Completed/Failed/Killed), the handler still returns 202 with the same body (idempotent no-op). Returns **400 Bad Request** with `error: "bad_request"` if `run_id` is not a valid UUID. Returns **404 Not Found** if the UUID is well-formed but no run exists.
}
